Z||000000||Jay||09-16-2001||10:30 PM||||Some may remember my last post where I ran a 13.6  Well Today I beat that time by 2/10th and ran a first ever 13.45<P>60' 1.99<BR>330 5.671<BR>1/8 8.646  mph 82.41<BR>1000 11.243<BR>1/4 13.450 @ 101.22mph<P>The only thing I did different was to keep the car in Overdrive rather than 3, and I let out about 5psi from the tires and ran the rears at 28psi.  Needless to say I'm thrilled about the time, I really  wasn't expecting to drop 2/10ths! Next week I think I  will start with the chip programmer.  This was achieved with a basically stock Northstar engine.  Can't wait to see what the modified chip will do.  I think high 12's will be a real possibility.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
