Z||000004||artherd||09-17-2001||05:48 AM||||Hi Jay, if you can find a way to fool the tranny computer into not telling the engine when it's going to shift, you should be able to pick up a good deal of time...<BR>(you probally know this, stated for reference)<BR>the tranny computer talks to the ECU, and cuts engine power (timing? injectors? spark?) during actual shifting, to smoothen said shifts.<P>How are you traction-limitation wise?<BR>(what tyres are you running?)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
