Z||000007||Jay||09-17-2001||12:50 PM||||Bandit I don't understand the reference to the S2000, I'm not worried about racing one!  Yes I've had to wear a helmet since last year when I hit 13.9  They know my car now so I always have to wear it.  There were 5 Fiero's there.  Mine (Northstar) an 84 with a 2.8 in it, a 2.8 turbo, another 2.8 turbo with intercooler and a 2.8 with a 30 shot of NOS.  The 2.8 turbo did a 15.4  The turbo with intercooler did a 13.8 I don't remember what the others did. <P>As far as traction, I'm not slipping at all at the line, at least very little tire spin.  I want to lighten the car not make it heavier.  Next time I may remove my trunk lid and passenger seat.  <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
